 "input": "presiding officer notes for polling day. collect the ballot box, ballot papers and the polling station register from the council the night before. open at 7am, show the empty box, seal it. voter gives name and address, poll clerk finds them on the register, checks photo ID, marks them off and writes their elector number on the corresponding number list (not on the ballot). hand ballot paper, voter goes to booth, puts paper in box. close at 10pm. complete the ballot paper account (issued, spoilt, unused), seal everything and take the box to the count. tendered ballots if someone already marked as voted.",
